        <entry morerows="2"> 01h 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col5"> Bit 0: Include_PCI_ALL If set the TSE engine includes all the PCIe devices in the specified segment. When there is multiple TSE capability reporting structures, this flag should only be set by the last TSCRS. Two TSCRS should not be setting this flag. If clear, this TSE only includes the ports in the specified segment as defined by the 'device scope' field. The device can be of any type as described by the 'Type' field. There can be more than 1 TCRS reported by BIOS with this flag set. BIOS needs to make sure that the devices in the device scope structure should not be linked to multiple TCRS. 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col5"> Bit 2: Virtualizable: Supports SRIOV or SIOV 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry> Bit 3: If Bit 2 is set, 0 = SRIOV, 1 = SIOV. if BIT2 is not set, Bit 3 should be 0 
